From: Nicholas Martin <nmartin0@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gold: include <string> explicitly in errors.h

Building gold with GCC 14 on Debian 13 fails:

    gold/errors.h:87:50: error: 'string' in namespace 'std' does not
        name a type
       87 |   undefined_symbol(const Symbol* sym, const std::string& location);
    note: 'std::string' is defined in header '<string>'; this is
          probably fixable by adding '#include <string>'

errors.h has used std::string since it was written, but never included
<string>.  It compiled because libstdc++ headers used to pull <string>
in transitively; they no longer do.  binutils 2.23.2 is from 2013, so
this was never noticed here.

The declaration is placed with <cstdarg>, matching the file's own
grouping of standard headers before local ones.

diff --git a/gold/errors.h b/gold/errors.h
--- a/gold/errors.h
+++ b/gold/errors.h
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #define GOLD_ERRORS_H
 
 #include <cstdarg>
+#include <string>
 
 #include "gold-threads.h"
 
